  "slug": "phosani-s-nightmare",
  "note": "Corrects a weights_sum failure caused by the wiki's own numbers, not a parser error (revid 15273922): the merged \"Runes and ammunition\"/\"Resources\"/\"Consumables\"/\"Coins\" heading's 25 rows are each individually written as a plain integer over a stated /100 (Cosmic rune 4/100 ... Coins 2/100), but the 25 numerators sum to 101, not 100 -- verified against the raw wikitext directly, transcribed verbatim, no row altered. There is no footnote, correction, or indication anywhere on the page of which single row's stated weight is the odd one out, so docking an arbitrary item by 1 to force a clean 100 would be a guess this project's own discipline rejects (see docs/DECISIONS.md's repeated refusals to invent a number the wiki doesn't state). Modelled instead as denominator 101 -- every row's own stated weight is kept EXACTLY as published, unchanged relative to every other row, and the reconciled total simply matches what the 25 rows actually sum to rather than the page's (evidently off-by-one) /100 label. This is the same principle already used throughout the corpus for a weighted table's denominator (the reconciled row total, not a literal transcription of the heading's own '/N' text) and is a roughly 1% correction, well inside the tolerance already accepted elsewhere for small wiki-side arithmetic slips (see Vorkath's accepted 1.6665x Seeds overshoot on the ambiguous-heading gate; this is the weights_sum analogue of the same kind of imprecision). Every other table is unchanged from the generated document.",
